"Zhipu Raises ~$5bn at HK$714, Half Its July Price (https://agenccy.ai/news/zhipu-is-raising-5bn-at-less-than-half-its-july-share-price/)\nciteturn773view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://agenccy.ai/news/zhipu-is-raising-5bn-at-less-than-half-its-july-share-price/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 118\nL0: cite0†AI News Today. Sep 15, 2026\nL1: \nL2: cite1†Latest cite2†Topics cite3†Companies cite4†Newsletter L3: \nL4: Data\nL5: \nL6: cite5†Company directory2,055 cite6†Case studies543 cite7†Funding tracker8,601 cite8†Compliance calendar63 L7: \nL8: Search news, companies, funding…\nL9: \nL10: [Input: Search news, companies, funding…]\nL11: \nL12: EN▼EN Englishcite9†ESEspañol cite10†PTPortuguês cite11†RUРусский cite12†ITItaliano cite13†FRFrançais cite14†ARالعربية cite15†ZH中文 cite16†KO한국어 L13: \nL14: cite17†Open Source AI L15: # Zhipu Is Raising $5bn at Less Than Half Its July Share Price\nL16: \nL17: The Hong Kong filing prices new shares at HK$714 against HK$1,588 nine weeks ago — and discloses that two thirds of the July money had not been spent.\nL18: \nL19: Sep 13, 2026 Source: cite18†HKEXnews†www1.hkexnews.hk L20: \nL21: cite19†Image: The masthead of the Hong Kong stock exchange filing itself: the Z.AI logo, the name Z.AI Co., Ltd. in English and Chinese, Stock Code 2513, the placing and convertible-bond headline, and CICC named as sole global coordinator. L22: ## Key Points\nL23: \nL24:   * 1.The placing is priced at HK$714.00, against HK$1,588.00 for the July placing completed on 13 July.\nL25:   * 2.HK$20.42bn of July's proceeds — 65.08% — was still unutilized as of 31 August.\nL26:   * 3.Both legs are conditional: the filing says the placing \"may or may not proceed\" and the bonds \"may or may not be issued\".\nL27: Z.AI Co., Ltd. — the Hong Kong-listed vehicle of the Chinese model lab Zhipu, stock code 2513 — filed on 13 September at 10:13 UTC to raise roughly US$5 billion across two instruments signed the previous day. The filing is the primary record and every figure below is read from it.\nL28: ## The two legs\nL29: \nL30: A placing of up to 21,965,000 new H shares at HK$714.00 — gross HK$15,683.01m, net HK$15,664.13m — to not fewer than six placees, none expected to become a substantial shareholder. Alongside it, RMB20.14 billion of US-dollar-settled zero-coupon convertible bonds due 2027, gross US$3,015.64m and net US$3,010.77m, converting at HK$892.50. The placing price is a 9.96% discount to the HK$793.00 close of 11 September; the conversion price a 12.55% premium to it.\nL31: ## What the money is for\nL32: \nL33: About 60% goes to next-generation GLM models, a system the company calls \"Fully Self Training\", and training and inference infrastructure; 15% to business expansion and possible acquisitions; 25% to capital structure and working capital.\nL34: ## The disclosure the coverage skipped\nL35: \nL36: The same document reports the July raise: 19,780,000 shares completed on 13 July at HK$1,588.00, netting HK$31,374.95m. As of 31 August, only HK$10,954.80m — 34.92% — had been used, leaving HK$20,420.15m unutilized. The company is raising again while sitting on roughly US$2.6bn of the last raise.\nL37: ## What the received framing gets wrong\nL38: Chinese headlines went out saying Zhipu had completed about US$5bn of financing. The filing says the opposite in terms: conditions precedent are unsatisfied, the managers hold termination rights, the placing \"may or may not proceed\", the bonds \"may or may not be issued\", and completion is scheduled for 16 September. Second, this is not \"a $5bn round\": roughly US$2bn is dilutive equity at a discount and US$3bn is debt that only becomes equity 25% higher, with no investor named and no venture money involved.\nL39: Third, \"Fully Self Training\" is a use-of-proceeds heading, not a capability — the filing says the company \"intends to explore\" a loop in which models help build their own training systems. There is no result behind it. And the price itself is the story being buried: at HK$714 the company issues more than twice as many shares per dollar as it did in July.\nL40: ## Why It Matters\nL41: \nL42: It is the largest single financing by a Chinese open-weight lab this year, priced off a share price that has more than halved since July, and the filing states plainly what the money buys: compute bought ahead of need, and the engineering to make mismatched generations of accelerators work together.\nL43: \nL44: ## More on this topic\nL45: \nL46:   * cite17†Open Source AI News L47:   * cite20†Finance AI News L48: \nL49: Filed undercite21†#Capital markets cite22†#China AI cite23†#Z.ai cite24†#Zhipu cite25†#open weights L50: ## Related Stories\nL51: \nL52:   * cite26†Ant Shipped Guardrail Probes for 27 Models, gpt-oss Included L53: \nL54: 1d ago · AI Safety\nL55: \nL56:   * cite27†Tencent's Sparse Attention Was Trained on Alibaba's Qwen3 L57: \nL58: 2d ago · AI Research\nL59: \nL60:   * cite28†Shanghai AI Lab Shipped 403B Weights With No Readable Scores L61: \nL62: 2d ago · AI Models\nL63: \nL64:   * cite29†Altman Ruled Out a 2026 IPO and Committed to No Other Year L65: \nL66: 2d ago · Finance AI\nL67: \nL68:   * cite30†Oracle Named AI in a $2.8bn Severance Plan It Filed on Friday Night L69: \nL70: 3d ago · Finance AI\nL71:   * cite31†Nvidia Is in Talks to Anchor Anthropic's IPO With Up to $10bn L72: \nL73: 3d ago · Nvidia\nL74: ### Data\nL75: \nL76:   * cite5†Company directory L77:   * cite6†Case studies L78:   * cite7†Funding tracker L79:   * cite8†Compliance calendar L80:   * cite32†Search L81: \nL82: ### Companies\nL83: \nL84:   * cite33†OpenAI News L85:   * cite34†Google AI News L86:   * cite35†Meta AI News L87:   * cite36†Nvidia AI News L88:   * cite37†Anthropic News L89: \nL90: ### Regulation\nL91: \nL92:   * cite38†AI Regulati